Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the EE clock waits split by the deadline that held them (TODO 295, only while TF_HITCH_MS > 0)

A slow frame's "waited for the clock" did not say what the EE was held for. The scheduler now adds each wait for the clock to the deadline it waited on (VBlankStart, VBlankEnd, a DMA channel, an alarm, the EE timer, or no deadline at all), and takeIdleBreakdown() hands the totals since the last call to the game's slow-frame line. The bookkeeping runs only while TF_HITCH_MS is above 0 (read once), so it costs nothing otherwise.

